        "original_id": "3ae8e622-7328-52f8-a05e-0437f2bb3eb8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Guggenheim Museum SoHo, Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum, Solomon R. Guggenheim Foundation, Fulcrum Gallery\n- People: Arata Isozaki, Hilla von Rebay, Valerie Monroe Shakespeare\n- Places: SoHo, Upper East Side, Manhattan, New York City\n- Roles: architect, first director\n\nFacts:\n- In 1939, the Solomon R. Guggenheim Foundation established the Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum as the Museum of Non-Objective Painting under the guidance of its first director, Hilla von Rebay.\n- The Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum is an art museum located at 1071 Fifth Avenue at East 89th Street in Manhattan's Upper East Side in New York City.\n- The Guggenheim Museum SoHo was a branch of the Guggenheim Museum designed by Arata Isozaki at Broadway and Prince Street in Manhattan's SoHo neighborhood in New York City.\n- In January 1993, Valerie Monroe Shakespeare opened Fulcrum Gallery beneath the Guggenheim Museum SoHo in New York City.\n- Fulcrum Gallery was also known as Shakespeare's Fvlcrvm or Fvlcrvm.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
